                <pb facs="0387" n="305" xml:id="pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.00/1188.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. McCreery says he is advised by the President of Honduras that Congress has
                    accepted the resignation of the Vice President, that Gen. Rafael López Gutiérrez
                    has been given command, and that Gen. Carias has ordered his troops to Comayagua
                    from Santa Cruz in accordance with peace agreement.</p>
            </div>
